{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "agile-af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068-dbb15742-0df1-4711-a3cb-520c4eb51c96", :event/time "2026-10-12T15:09:38.883Z", :session/id "agile", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068", :dependency nil, :parent nil, :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1791817778874-0.ncyop7770rstm8s6qvf", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Standard event IDs and script-facing ledger integrity checks", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/cephalon-rheos-event-epic/rheos/docs/agile/tasks/standard-event-ids-and-script-facing-ledger-integrity-checks-a75d5068.md", :status "incoming", :epic nil, :body "## Context\n\nThe human authorized the historical row repair on 2026-10-12: \"You can fix the ledger rows. We should probably have a check for that on the scripts, and a standard way of creating and checking the ids\". Muse PR6 retains two distinct title/labels events at ledger rows 76 and 77 with one event/id. Rheos PR16 already replaced timestamp-only event generation with UUID generation, but there is no reusable ID construction/check contract or script-facing ledger identity check.\n\n## Outcome\n\nOne standard Rheos event-ID construction and validation boundary is used by the producer and available to scripts/CI. The explicitly authorized Muse data correction makes both existing records independently addressable and retains their original bytes and source revisions as provenance.\n\n## Scope\n\nExtract the existing board/task/UUID event-ID composition into a reusable portable shape/law boundary. Keep entropy generation at the runtime edge. Add a read-only canonical Rheos CLI check that reads every event ledger row, rejects malformed/non-map records and missing/non-string/blank IDs, and reports every duplicate with one-based row locations. Preserve compatible opaque legacy IDs; validation must not require rewriting distinct historical timestamp-based IDs. Event IDs identify individual records; write IDs remain correlation values shared by one multi-field operation.\n\nThe owning consumer applies only the two explicitly authorized event/id changes. Archive the exact original two lines, original Git blob/commit, full ledger SHA256 and before/after row hashes, preserving row order, record count, every other field and all other row bytes. This specific human authorization is an exception for these two data corrections, not a standing permission to rewrite receipts or history. Add a consumer CI invocation of the qualified canonical check through a revision-bound Rheos source; do not create a second Muse/Foresight validator.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo runtime restart, deployment, live publication, unrelated board transitions, deduplication/deletion, broad historical migration, causal-root/write-ID changes, dependency upgrade, alternate identity authority, general-purpose ledger repair protocol or extra review-policy waiver.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. The producer uses the shared constructor and generated IDs have a validated UUID suffix with the existing board/task prefix. Invalid creation inputs fail explicitly. Frozen time and two independent real writers retain distinct event IDs; existing event meanings and persistence-before-publication stay intact.\n2. The read-only canonical check accepts unique compatible opaque IDs, including legacy timestamp IDs. It detects identical and different-payload duplicate records, missing/null/boolean/blank IDs, non-map data and malformed input with exact physical row numbers. It never silently skips an unreadable row or counts a partial scan as success.\n3. The CLI has documented stable success/failure exits and makes no board/card/ledger write while checking, including missing/unreadable input and invalid-data cases. Scripts invoke this owner rather than reimplementing identity rules.\n4. The real Muse rows 76 and 77 are corrected under the quoted authorization. Original raw rows remain recoverable; all original payloads, timestamps, write IDs and causal roots remain byte-identical, and all 78 other original rows remain byte-identical and in order. The qualified canonical check verifies the complete corrected ledger.\n5. Consumer CI pins and invokes the reviewed owner. A deliberately duplicated fixture fails the same checker and a unique compatible fixture passes. The consumer's ordinary gates and fresh exact-head review/settlement qualify its new revision.\n\n## Verification\n\nPlanning review and native Ready precede source implementation. Commit meaningful failing law/CLI tests first, then green portable semantics and outer adapters. Run full existing lint/test/build gates with zero compiler/lint warnings. Exercise actual checker process exits and unchanged fixture bytes, full real ledger validation and negative replay/index fixtures. Record exact input/output/source hashes and actual review IDs. No local test or source plan stands in for native source qualification or live character proof.\n\n## Risks\n\nA syntax reader can accept only a prefix unless whole-row consumption is checked. A uniqueness-only check must not claim complete event-schema validity. Random UUIDs are collision-resistant, so the check remains necessary. Changing original identifiers may affect an external ID-based reference; the correction manifest must retain original identity and exact row binding. The two original events shared a write ID legitimately; changing it would destroy correlation. Existing malformed history outside the authorized pair must be reported separately rather than silently rewritten.\n\nProcess documentation: GPL-3.0-or-later."}, :causal/root "2d66a29e-2e97-4aa3-8e44-ed240920cf5d"}
{:event/type "kanban.frontmatter", :event/id "agile-af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068-de03f016-1f7a-4dfe-a816-447f1f5faa62", :event/time "2026-10-12T15:25:21.512Z", :session/id "agile", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068", :key "points", :old-value "5", :new-value "3", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1791818721501-0.l0yxqop5gbvx6uo11p", :type "frontmatter"}, :causal/root "ade9eed8-1038-49f1-840a-f159a5699f3b"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "agile-adopt-qualified-event-id-checks-in-the-muse-consumer-7268b4b6-356c-483b-b6d1-3d4f77004d55", :event/time "2026-10-12T15:25:30.068Z", :session/id "agile", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "adopt-qualified-event-id-checks-in-the-muse-consumer", :dependency ["af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068"], :parent nil, :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1791818730059-0.ztb8eohw33ck66he87w", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Adopt qualified event-ID checks in the Muse consumer", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/cephalon-rheos-event-epic/rheos/docs/agile/tasks/adopt-qualified-event-id-checks-in-the-muse-consumer.md", :status "incoming", :epic nil, :body "## Context\n\nThe human authorized the two colliding Muse ledger-row corrections and requested standard creation/checking plus script checks. Muse commit8acedb549a93c7a97634f9f40a4844a34e3285e3 already corrects event IDs in physical rows76/77 and retains original raw rows, source Git blob and exact hashes. Rheos owner taskaf67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068 separately supplies the future constructor/checker. This rollout card is recorded on the same coordinating Rheos board so its UUID dependency is native and checkable; implementation and the consumer PR remain in personal Muse.\n\n## Outcome\n\nMuse scripts/CI invoke the qualified revision-bound Rheos owner checker on the active ledger, and the complete corrected ledger passes. Owner completion does not depend on this consumer rollout completing.\n\n## Scope\n\nRetain the expressly authorized two-row correction and original-row custody. After the owner implementation is qualified and its card Done, pin its exact reviewed source/release and invoke its canonical CLI/script API from Muse CI. Add a deliberately duplicated owned fixture that fails that same owner and a unique compatible legacy fixture that passes. The actual active ledger must pass the canonical check. Record actual checker/process exits and source/input hashes, and qualify the consumer change with full ordinary gates and fresh exact-head reviews.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo Muse/Foresight parser or validator, ledger deduplication/deletion, broad migration, timestamp/causal-root/write-ID changes, owner gate bypass, namespace-loss CLI repair, provider/model/credential changes, runtime/deployment/publication, field/mood completion or general-purpose history-repair protocol.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Original two rows, immutable source commit/blob, before/after ledger hashes and old/new row bindings remain recoverable. The correction changes only two ID strings; the other78 original rows and all non-ID fields/order/count remain exact. Subsequent provenance appends are distinct new records, not a false claim that the complete corrected head equals its older prefix.\n2. Dependency af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068 is retained. Consumer adoption begins only after qualified owner implementation and native Done, never from a planning approval alone. Pin the actual qualified source/release and verify that invocation uses that binding.\n3. Consumer CI checks an explicit active-ledger path through the owner. It does not recursively scan custody archives: original-rows.edn intentionally preserves the old duplicate IDs. Missing/unreadable/empty/malformed/duplicate data fail through the owner contract with nonzero exits.\n4. A duplicate fixture fails and a unique compatible legacy fixture passes the exact same owner API; both fixture bytes remain unchanged. The complete real corrected Muse ledger passes, with actual report and source/input SHA retained. This is ID integrity, not full event-schema or Mongo import proof.\n5. The consumer's normal CI/build/lint/tool gates and fresh current-head source reviews/settlements qualify an ordinary history-preserving MERGE. Approval, cohort and completion do not transfer from the owner. Owning Muse transport readiness and B1/B2/liveB3 remain separate.\n\n## Verification\n\nThis is a separate two-point consumer rollout estimate, dependent on the three-point owner story; the split retains the original total five-point estimate. Estimates remain provisional for independent planning review. Native Ready precedes committed consumer RED/GREEN controls. Preserve both the raw historical archive and all receipt/reflection prefixes. No local demonstration or source plan supplies qualified adoption or live character completion.\n\n## Risks\n\nA wrong target path can pass only if the checker wrongly accepts missing/empty data; owner refusal tests remain mandatory. Original ID-based external references may exist, so original bindings and hashes must remain visible. A copied validator or unqualified owner pin would fork authority. Provider review outages are not quota or approval evidence.\n\nProcess documentation: GPL-3.0-or-later."}, :causal/root "35b07d63-867d-4471-9fe4-2bc39eb6b949"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "agile-af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068-287b05ed-859f-4fc3-b8a2-c391fc7708e8", :event/time "2026-10-12T15:47:04.215Z", :session/id "agile", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068", :text "Current owner-body revision snapshot; original task-created body remains immutable history. At source 0fa2c8fa6b81ec04280f0311ab8a035865d72f69, owner af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068 is Incoming/3points and consumer adopt-qualified-event-id-checks-in-the-muse-consumer is Incoming/2points with this owner dependency. The initial combined five-point body is superseded as current scope by the separately reviewed Markdown revision below. This canonical comment captures that complete current body in the append-only native history. It supplies no new replay engine, automatic body projection, planning approval, Ready transition or implementation. Snapshot UTF8 bytes=7304; SHA256=946f94dc53b495cfe59264f1a3067155ab67cea1390c5ad30ab76a6752fde836.\n\nBEGIN CURRENT OWNER BODY\n## Context\n\nThe human authorized the historical row repair on 2026-10-12: \"You can fix the ledger rows. We should probably have a check for that on the scripts, and a standard way of creating and checking the ids\". Muse PR6 at immutable cd5c4d5372aede740feeed74554f635a08559b09 had two distinct title/labels events at ledger rows76/77 with one event/id; the separately authorized correction is now committed at8acedb549a93c7a97634f9f40a4844a34e3285e3 with original-row custody. Rheos PR16 already replaced timestamp-only generation with UUID generation, but there is no reusable construction/check contract or script-facing ledger identity check.\n\n## Outcome\n\nOne portable Rheos owner module supplies distinct generated-ID and retained-ledger-ID contracts, used by the producer and available to scripts/CI. This owner card can complete after its own source qualification and publication; the dependent consumer rollout has separate acceptance and review gates.\n\n## Scope\n\nExtract the existing board/task/UUID composition into a deterministic portable constructor accepting explicit board ID, task ID and UUID entropy. Board/task components preserve the exact nonblank identity strings already allowed by configured board IDs and stored task references, including legacy opaque punctuation, embedded whitespace and Unicode; do not apply new-card filename-safe or RFC UUID restrictions to those components or trim/normalize them. Reject blank or non-string components. Keep entropy generation at the runtime edge. Name separate generated-ID validation (the producer's prefix plus canonical UUID suffix) and ledger-admission validation (compatible nonblank opaque IDs, with uniqueness checked over all physical records). Add a read-only canonical CLI check that reads every physical ledger line, refuses incomplete or extra forms and invalid/non-map records, and reports duplicate IDs with exact one-based row locations. Dispatch this explicit-path check before general CLI board/config/view bootstrap, so unrelated configuration cannot decide its ledger-specific result. Event IDs identify records; write IDs remain correlation values shared by a multi-field operation.\n\nExport the checker through the owning CLI/script boundary and document invocation and revision binding. The separate two-point consumer card `adopt-qualified-event-id-checks-in-the-muse-consumer` depends on owner UUID `af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068` on this same coordinating board; its implementation and PR belong in personal Muse. This three-point owner plus the two-point rollout retain the original five-point total provisionally. The dependent consumer card covers the already authorized Muse correction, its original-row archive and consumer CI pin/adoption after this owner implementation is qualified. Owner release and consumer adoption do not transfer approval or completion to each other; no Muse/Foresight validator is introduced.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo runtime restart, deployment, live publication, unrelated board transitions, deduplication/deletion, broad historical migration, causal-root/write-ID changes, dependency upgrade, alternate identity authority, general-purpose ledger repair protocol or extra review-policy waiver.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Identical explicit constructor inputs return the identical generated ID; changing valid UUID entropy changes the ID. Blank/non-string board/task components and invalid UUID entropy refuse; nonblank opaque board/task strings retain exactly the existing emission identity domain, including `literal, id`, punctuation, internal whitespace and Unicode. Generated-ID validation checks the prefix against explicit expected board/task components and canonical UUID entropy, without an ambiguous hyphen split or new-card filename restriction. Constructor and actual emission adapter controls include those legacy opaque board/task inputs and unchanged exact components. The production adapter obtains fresh entropy for each emission before calling the constructor; controlled adapter tests observe that boundary. Frozen time and two independent real writers retain distinct event IDs, unchanged non-ID fields and persistence-before-publication.\n2. Ledger admission independently accepts unique compatible opaque strings, including timestamp-based legacy IDs, without applying generated-ID UUID restrictions. It refuses identical and different-payload duplicates, missing/null/boolean/blank/non-string IDs and non-map records with exact physical row numbers. An ID check does not claim full event-schema admission.\n3. Each physical line must contain exactly one complete EDN form. Two forms on one line, a form spanning lines, trailing forms/junk and blank or comment-only physical lines refuse. A single terminal LF or CRLF is a record terminator rather than another blank row; extra blank lines refuse. A zero-byte file refuses rather than passing as an empty scan. No malformed line is silently skipped or partial scan treated as success.\n4. CLI outcomes bind the existing exit contract: unique nonempty input exits0, missing path exits2, malformed/invalid/duplicate/empty input exits3, unreadable input or other I/O failure exits4, and missing command arguments exit1. Every failure exits nonzero. The explicit-path check bypasses board configuration discovery/loading/resolution and view-store bootstrap before dispatch. Real process controls invoke it from a directory with no board config and with an unrelated malformed or unreadable `KANBAN_CONFIG`; those unrelated inputs do not alter its ledger-specific outcome. Preserve fixture bytes and prove no board/config/card/ledger creation or write on any check path, including missing/unreadable input.\n5. The public owner invocation accepts an explicit active-ledger path, has stable documented result fields and uses the same portable ID rules as production. Owner script/CLI tests include a duplicate negative and unique compatible positive. Full source gates and exact-head review qualify the owner revision before the separate consumer pins/adopts it; the owner can complete independently.\n\n## Verification\n\nPlanning review and native Ready precede source implementation. Commit meaningful failing law/CLI tests first, then green portable semantics and outer adapters. Run full existing lint/test/build gates with zero compiler/lint warnings. Exercise constructor determinism and adapter entropy, strict per-line EOF/blank/empty controls, actual process exits and unchanged fixture bytes. Record exact input/output/source hashes and actual review IDs. Consumer ledger validation and adoption remain separately gated; no owner test/source plan supplies live character proof.\n\n## Risks\n\nA syntax reader can accept only a prefix unless whole-row consumption is checked. A uniqueness-only check must not claim complete event-schema validity. Random UUIDs are collision-resistant, so the check remains necessary. Changing original identifiers may affect an external ID-based reference; the correction manifest must retain original identity and exact row binding. The two original events shared a write ID legitimately; changing it would destroy correlation. Existing malformed history outside the authorized pair must be reported separately rather than silently rewritten.\n\nProcess documentation: GPL-3.0-or-later.\nEND CURRENT OWNER BODY", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1791820024212-0.jg9yd0m95ulo1o2upr", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "8c845179-778b-40c2-8f0b-9683ac9ecc60"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "agile-af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068-8162e317-bf7e-412b-862c-76146c0ef2c9", :event/time "2026-10-12T19:09:06.750Z", :session/id "agile", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "af67891c-fbb4-4f40-a6a2-e9bda75d5068", :text "Planning is qualified and merged in personal Rheos PR18 at 14913881d7ae025b982d5cf583bfeefdcbec9f64, preserving exact reviewed head 220acdc3ce8c4abf8df74a0da6a85fc09dfcb944. The independently reviewed three-point owner will now proceed through native readiness and RED before portable identity and explicit-path read-only checker implementation. Consumer adoption remains dependent and unimplemented. No live cephalon, model, inference credential or runtime change.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1791832146747-0.l9ef5m175a8wkeezncl", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "26818fbe-4d87-478a-9ba1-8cefda44ed54"}
